# 04g-joint-allocation -- verdict, iteration 1

Chapter: book/04g-joint-allocation.qmd (1,321 lines). Read in full, with R/18_joint_allocation.R, R/17 (sparse_alloc, sparse_vc), tests/testthat/test-joint.R, the `joint` block of book/scripts/regenerate.R, the three book/data/joint_*.csv, it1-audit.md, it1-refs.md, it1-continuity.md, THREAD.md (lines naming 04g), 04e it3-verdict (OPEN) and 04f it3-verdict (approved; 04f not judged). Computation in scratchpad .../scratchpad/v/ (cap.R, par.R, ct.R, r8.R, r11.R, rep.R, orc.R), package loaded with pkgload::load_all of the worktree.

VERDICT: REJECTED

PREVIOUS IDS (re-review only)
- Not applicable (iteration 1). The audit R, refs B and continuity C findings are consumed below; their status in 04g-D/M numbering is in the cross-table at the end.

DISQUALIFYING FAILURES

- 04g-D1 [criteria 5, 7] 04g:79-80, 04g:1021, 04g:1061-1065 (and R/18 roxygen, 04f:1277) -- `coverage` is declared the `parentage` allocation of @sec-sparse "under another name". It is not the same allocation. Recomputed on the complete 20 x 20 factorial, 8 locations, k = 2, seeds 1..20 (par.R): `all(Mc == Mp)` is FALSE in 20 of 20 draws; both give fem_cover = male_cover = 1 and equal loads, but frac_disconn is 0 (coverage) against 0.286 (parentage) in 20 of 20 draws, conc_hmean about 13.4 against 0 (structural: nM x k = 20 group-location memberships cover at most 20 of 28 location pairs, R/17:84-89). R/17 `parentage` cuts the factorial into nM cyclic groups and optimises concurrence; R/18 `coverage` is a greedy parent-presence rule with no concurrence term. 04f result 4 is exactly about parentage sharing no hybrid between some location pairs, so the identification changes what is being compared. Consequence: the chapter reads its coverage-minus-random contrast as "consistent with" 04f's parentage-minus-random finding (04g:1061-1065) and treats it as the 04f hypothesis in action (D3). "Plays the same role" would be defensible; "under another name" is false. (Audit R6, continuity C2.)

- 04g-D2 [criteria 5, 7] 04g:49-50 and 04g:127-128 against 04g:989-992 -- the chapter says @sec-sparse took "the whole factorial as given" and varied k "at fixed n_c = n_F n_M". 04f:207-212, 1233-1236 and limitation 7 (04f:1843) state that 80 % of the hybrids are planted (about 16 planted crosses per line), so n_c = 320 there. 04g:989-992 says "the planted 80 % of the factorial" correctly. The chapter contradicts itself and its source in the two places that frame the problem and the budget identity (eq-joint-budget) (R/18 header, lines 3-5, repeats it). (Continuity C1.)

- 04g-D3 [criteria 4, 3] 04g:1298-1300 -- "the hypothesis of result 4 ... turned into an allocation rule and tested here". Recomputed (ct.R): coverage - random on acc_all, 24 cells, +0.0057 +/- 0.0033, z 1.74, 16 of 24 positive; circulant 12 cells z 1.79, random 8 cells z 2.29, tester 4 cells z -1.14; 2 of 24 cells |z| > 2 (2.32, 2.68). That contrast is at fixed plan, k and loads and moves parent coverage and shared-hybrid concurrence together (D1), so it cannot separate the mechanism result 4 of 04f left open; a non-detection at z 1.74 is not a test of a hypothesis. "Tested here" presents an interpretation as a result. (Audit R7, continuity C3.)

- 04g-D4 [criterion 3] 04g:67-71 (result 1) -- "by a margin that grows with the specific combining ability (SCA) variance". The only evidence is two SCA levels and point estimates. Recomputed from joint_core_sweep.csv (r8.R), 160-vs-40 difference, coverage, circulant: h2 0.2 low 0.064, high 0.096, difference of differences 0.032, s.e. 0.038, z 0.86; h2 0.4 low 0.087, high 0.146, 0.059, s.e. 0.030, z 1.98. Not detected at h2 0.2, borderline at 0.4; and at h2 0.2 the 80-vs-40 step is smaller with high SCA (0.052 low, 0.013 high). The cells are independent, so the s.e. was available and not computed. A comparative headline claim without the uncertainty that its own data allow. (Audit R8.)

- 04g-D5 [criterion 7] 04g:365-367 -- "Sparse factorials train hybrid prediction at least as well as tester designs, and fewer crosses per line favours the lines never crossed [@seye2020; @lorenzi2022; @melchinger2023]". quant-refcheck (04g-B1, WRONG, abstract level): Seye et al. 2020 report a small impact of the contribution number per line; Melchinger et al. 2023 show the symmetric cost (c = 1 lowest accuracy for H1, H2 and GCA of I1 lines; optimum "depends on the size and resources of the breeding program"). The Melchinger side is consistent with what 04e it3 verified from the Europe PMC full text (04e it3 verdict, D16); I did not read Seye or Lorenzi myself and take their side from refcheck's abstract quotations. The sentence is unconditional where 04e, after three iterations, conditions the same claim on c, layout and estimator (continuity C15), and omits the trade-off that result 1 of this chapter turns on. Attribution broader than the sources.

NON-DISQUALIFYING OBSERVATIONS

- 04g-M1 04g:1277-1279 and R/18:20-21 (audit R1, R2, continuity C19) -- the coverage rule does not hold "no location may exceed ceiling(n k / nLoc)". Recomputed over 100 seeds per sweep configuration, coverage allocation (cap.R): seeds 1..100 gave 20/100 violations at circulant c = 2, k = 4 and 2/100 at c = 4, k = 2 (the audit's figures reproduce); seeds 101..200 gave 18/100, 3/100, plus 4/100 at random c = 4 and 1/100 at the tester design; max excess 1 everywhere (cap 20, one location with 21). The test list says the rule "balances loads and covers more of each pool"; test-joint.R:17-24 checks load balance at k = 1 only and female coverage only. Effect on the sweep is one plot at one location; the chapter does not state the cap, so it is not a result claim, but the package text and the test description overstate.
- 04g-M2 04g:950-955 (audit R9) -- "two-tester design sits below the circulant c = 4 plan in every scenario and strategy" has no z in the text. Recomputed (r8.R): all 16 pairs (4 scenarios x 4 strategies) are below, z -2.1 to -3.8, so the statement holds in direction and mostly past two s.e. The plans also differ in n_crosses (76 vs 80) and in line structure; no causal reading to the testers is made. Report z or say "point estimates".
- 04g-M3 04g:957-975 and tbl-joint-made (audit R10) -- acc_made is cor over the crosses made, which are different subsets (160, 80, 40 of 400) at each split, and the reversal is explained "because each is seen in four locations": a mechanism read off a design contrast in which n_c and k change together. Estimand non-comparability not said. Independent replication with fresh seeds (rep.R, seed 777, h2 0.4, 30 replicates): the reversal is reproduced in direction (made 0.806 vs 0.868, z 5.3 low SCA; 0.726 vs 0.855, z 9.5 high SCA), larger than the chapter's 0.807 vs 0.845 (z 2.67), so the chapter is not overstating it.
