WHAT WAS VERIFIED

- Cap violation -- cap.R, coverage allocation, 100 seeds per configuration (20 x 20, 8 locations): seeds 1..100, circulant c = 2, k = 4: 20/100, c = 4, k = 2: 2/100 (audit figures), max excess 1; seeds 101..200: 18/100 and 3/100, random c = 4 4/100, tester 1/100, others 0; max excess 1. The audit's "other four configurations 0" holds on seeds 1..100 only; other seeds show it is not specific to the two named configurations.
- Parentage vs coverage -- par.R, complete 20 x 20, 8 locations, k = 2, seeds 1..20: allocations differ in 20/20; fem_cover = male_cover = 1 both; load range 0 both; frac_disconn 0 vs 0.286 in 20/20; conc_hmean 12.3 to 13.9 (coverage) vs 0.
- Planted 80 % -- 04f:208, 1233-1236, 1591, 1843 read: 20 x 20, 80 % planted, about 16 planted crosses per line.
- Coverage minus random on acc_all -- ct.R from joint_contrasts.csv: 24 cells, +0.005695 +/- 0.003272, z 1.741, 16/24 positive; families circulant +0.0075 (z 1.79), random +0.0119 (z 2.29), tester -0.0123 (z -1.14); |z| > 2 in 2 cells (2.32, 2.68). optimised - start: +0.00266 +/- 0.00222; tester +0.0189 +/- 0.0070, z 2.71, 4/4 positive. All as printed in the chapter.
- Budget-split steps -- r8.R: z 160v80 0.51, 1.15, 3.41, 2.14; 80v40 1.86, 3.37, 0.48, 4.38 (4 under 2, one at 2.14, as the chapter says); coverage cell means 0.787/0.767/0.700 and 0.682/0.636/0.535 (h2 0.4) reproduced.
- Independent Monte Carlo replication (rep.R, seed 777, fresh draws, circulant plans, h2 0.4, 30 replicates): low SCA coverage 0.783 > 0.741 > 0.709 (z 160v40 4.52), high SCA 0.671 > 0.613 > 0.572 (z 4.67); coverage - random per configuration +0.013, -0.003, -0.010 (s.e. 0.010-0.013) and +0.005, -0.009, -0.011: none detected. Direction of result 1 and non-detection in result 2 are reproduced; this is a replication with other seeds, not a rerun of the cached CSV.
- joint_connectivity oracle -- orc.R: independent label-propagation oracle for n_comp_cross and n_comp_loc on 150 random allocations (random sparse, circulant, two disconnected NC II blocks; k 1 or 2; a location blanked in about 30 %): 0 mismatches, 93 with n_comp_cross > 1 and 17 with n_comp_loc > 1; no counterexample to "every location has a plot and n_comp_cross = 1 imply n_comp_loc = 1". Alias example: both counts 1, rank 3 of 4 columns.
- g_target shared between allocations with the same seed -- identical(a$g_target, b$g_target) TRUE (pairing claim holds).
- Identities by algebra: eq-joint-ssb, eq-joint-gd, eq-joint-gdbs, eq-joint-base, per-marker GD(p0) - GD(pbar) = 2(p0 - pbar)(1 - p0 - pbar), E[SS_B] share (L-1)/(N_P-1) = 7/159; coverage ceiling for testers (18 x 4/8 + 2)/20 = 0.55; Caballero & Toro form confirmed against it1-refs (full text). The chunk's stopifnot() assertions passed in the audit's knit.
- Uncrossed-line share -- exact per-line P = 0.0102 gives 0.336 (c = 4) and 0.0010 (c = 8); Monte Carlo 4000 draws 0.3545; chapter 0.348 and 0.001.
- PEV spread and timings -- 0.33 / 1.82 / 4.68 % reproduced; coverage 1.9 ms, joint_pev 129 ms; the 21 optimiser times below 600 s sum to 16.43 min (median 46.7 s).
- Spearman n = 6 exact critical 0.886 (chapter 0.89, p minimum 2/720).

